<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brandub mac Echach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 605</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brandub mac Echach was a King of Leinster of the Uí Chennselaig. In 598 he defeated and killed the high king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aed-mac-ainmuirech">Áed mac Ainmuirech</a> of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dun-bolg">Battle of Dún Bolg</a>, a victory long celebrated in Leinster tradition. He was killed in 605, and his family's later kings ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferns">Ferns</a>.</p></div>
